-- title:
--   λ-series generates the level-4 modular function field
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure. Inside the field of Laurent series $L((q))$ (formal Hahn series over $L$ with value group $\mathbb{Z}$), two intermediate fields over $L$ are compared. The first is `IntermediateField.adjoin L {lambdaModC L}`, generated over $L$ by the single series `lambdaModC L`, the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Z} \to L$ of the integral series `lambdaInt` $= q \cdot \mathrm{etaProd}^{8} \cdot \mathrm{qExpand}\,4\,(\mathrm{etaProd}^{16}) \cdot \mathrm{qExpand}\,2\,(\mathrm{dedekindEtaUnitInv})$, where `qExpand R n` is the substitution $q \mapsto q^{n}$. The second is `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull 4)`: writing `coeffEmb L` for the coefficientwise embedding $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, it is the subfield of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the image under `coeffEmb L` of `modularFunctionFieldFull 4`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,(\mathrm{jq})$ for the nonzero divisors $d \mid 4$, i.e. by $j(q)$, $j(q^{2})$ and $j(q^{4})$. The assertion is that these two intermediate fields of $L((q))/L$ coincide.
--
--   This expresses the classical fact that $\mu = \lambda/16$ (with $\lambda$ Legendre's modular function, evaluated after the substitution $\tau \mapsto 2\tau$) is a Hauptmodul of the genus-zero curve $X_0(4)$, in the purely formal setting of $q$-expansions: the $q$-series attached to $\mu$ generates, over any field of characteristic zero, exactly the field generated by $j(q), j(q^2), j(q^4)$. It is used for the statements placing `lambdaModC` in the level-4 modular function field, and for computations of relative degrees of the fields obtained by adjoining $\lambda$-series of higher level.
